_count":5},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":5},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Pubs, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKoQ","review_id":"ccPRFJUy8jsZBjNZn_-isA","date":"2016-07-20T18:10:21","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9316954612731934,"text_excerpt":"Great location right in the heart of French Quarter. The restaurant is big, and has three floors to it. There was a live band playing music when we arrived during lunchtime, which set a nice ambience for us to enjoy our meal. I felt bad that more people weren't seated in front of the band though - they way each room branches off, the band was basically playing to an empty space. They do have outdoor seating on the balcony which makes for a nice place to people watch, if you're lucky and can avoid any of the thunderstorms that frequently come out of nowhere. Food and beer were also pretty good. If/when I come back to NOLA, I'd come back to Jax."},{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKoQ","review_id":"v35rXfCXpCLHySIchT0NMA","date":"2016-12-12T04:31:17","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9268879890441895,"text_excerpt":"This is a fun little pub with a great selection of local brews! It's very conveniently located close to the French Quarter and the service was very good. The beer was great and they have flights, which is always what I like. We tried buffalo frog legs as well and I wouldn't eat them again, but I think that's just because I didn't enjoy frog legs in general. I would definitely come back here again!"},{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKoQ","review_id":"eHscV4MgEGr3NHFhthb47Q","date":"2016-12-12T01:58:02","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9245489835739136,"text_excerpt":"Jax Brewhouse exceeded our expectations. We stopped by for dinner. It's 3 stories talk with a converted open, modern loft feel. We were fatties on our last night in NOLA and ordered an app and entree each. I ordered the Buffalo frog legs and a fried oyster Rockefeller po boy. The frog legs had a southern fried texture with a dash of Buffalo sauce. They were very good. The po boy had fresh baked bread and was very large. It was a pleasant surprise. The wife like her fried green tomatoes and brisket sandwich. The menu is small, but it seems they keep the mantra of less us more and focus on quality. I recommend coming here if you want a change of food pace from the French Quarter but don't w..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKoQ","photo_id":"XmBymq2k1enfBVJtoXjH_A","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/XmBymq2k1enfBVJtoXjH_A.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9415854811668396},{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKoQ","photo_id":"Sk951MkGrmvnWFQwK8FeDA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Sk951MkGrmvnWFQwK8FeDA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8502843379974365},{"business_id":"nj_6YtupsFwSp8xYYyWKo